{"Title":"An Act to allow students access to prescription cannabis","BillNumber":"S59","DocketNumber":"SD1699","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"SLM0","Name":"Susan L. Moran","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SLM0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T14:55:13.603"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"SLM0","Name":"Susan L. Moran","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SLM0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T14:55:13.6033333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S59/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Moran, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 59) of Susan L. Moran for legislation to allow students access to prescription cannabis.  Cannabis Policy.","DocumentText":"\tSection 2 of chapter 94G of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting, after the word “facility”, in line 41, the following:-\r\n\t“; provided, however, that this paragraph shall not apply to possession or consumption of medical use marijuana as defined in chapter 94I; or (4) authorize the possession or consumption of marijuana or marijuana accessories”.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J50","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J50"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}